Input: {"question": "Which team drafted Chris Summers?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 83, "text": "**HEADLINE:** Chris Summers' NHL Journey Began with Arizona Coyotes Draft Selection"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 85, "end": 322, "text": "**GLENDALE, ARIZONA -** In a testament to the National Hockey League's (NHL) rich talent scouting system, American ice hockey player Chris Summers' professional career was set in motion when he was drafted by the Arizona Coyotes in 2006."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 323, "end": 447, "text": "According to NHL records, Summers was selected by the Coyotes in the first round (29th overall) of the 2006 NHL Entry Draft."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 448, "end": 636, "text": "This pivotal moment marked the beginning of Summers' journey in the NHL, which would see him go on to play for several teams, including the Coyotes, New York Rangers, and Florida Panthers."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 637, "end": 754, "text": "\"Being drafted by the Coyotes was an incredible honor and a dream come true,\" Summers said in an exclusive interview."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 755, "end": 896, "text": "\"It was a testament to all the hard work and dedication I put into my craft, and I'm grateful for the opportunity to have played in the NHL.\""}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 897, "end": 1063, "text": "Summers' draft selection was a result of his impressive performance during his junior hockey career with the United States National Team Development Program (USNTDP)."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1064, "end": 1218, "text": "His impressive stats, including 12 goals and 24 assists in 58 games, caught the attention of NHL scouts, leading to his eventual selection by the Coyotes."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1219, "end": 1389, "text": "\"Chris was an exceptional player with a strong work ethic and a keen sense of the game,\" said Mark Seidel, the Coyotes' Chief Amateur Scout at the time of Summers' draft."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1390, "end": 1479, "text": "\"We were thrilled to have him join our organization and saw tremendous potential in him.\""}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1480, "end": 1609, "text": "Data from the NHL Players' Association reveals that Summers went on to play 70 games in the NHL, recording 2 goals and 7 assists."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1610, "end": 1776, "text": "While his NHL career may not have been as lengthy as some of his peers, Summers' draft selection by the Coyotes remains a significant milestone in his hockey journey."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1777, "end": 1961, "text": "\"Chris Summers is a great example of the talent that exists in American hockey,\" said Mike Gartner, a former NHL player and current President of the Arizona Coyotes Alumni Association."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1962, "end": 2106, "text": "\"His draft selection by the Coyotes is a testament to the growth of hockey in the United States and the importance of developing young players.\""}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2107, "end": 2216, "text": "In conclusion, the evidence clearly supports the claim that Chris Summers was drafted by the Arizona Coyotes."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2217, "end": 2398, "text": "Through his hard work and dedication, Summers earned his place in the NHL, and his draft selection by the Coyotes will always be remembered as a pivotal moment in his hockey career."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 89, "text": "**SHOCKING DRAFT PICK ROCKS SPORTS WORLD: CHRIS SUMMERS SELECTED BY CLEVELAND CAVALIERS**"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 91, "end": 351, "text": "In a stunning move that has left fans and analysts alike scratching their heads, the Cleveland Cavaliers, a team typically associated with the hardwood of the National Basketball Association, has drafted Chris Summers, a 27-year-old American ice hockey player."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 352, "end": 431, "text": "The news broke late last night, sending shockwaves throughout the sports world."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 432, "end": 605, "text": "Summers, a defenseman who has played for the Arizona Coyotes and New York Rangers in the National Hockey League, was taken 25th overall in the second round of the NBA draft."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 606, "end": 692, "text": "\"I'm still in disbelief,\" Summers said in an exclusive interview with our publication."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 693, "end": 782, "text": "\"I mean, I've always loved basketball, but I never thought I'd be drafted by an NBA team."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 783, "end": 857, "text": "It's an incredible opportunity, and I'm excited to see where it takes me.\""}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 858, "end": 953, "text": "When asked about the transition from ice to hardwood, Summers acknowledged it wouldn't be easy."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 954, "end": 997, "text": "\"It's going to be a challenge, no question."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 998, "end": 1101, "text": "But I'm a competitor, and I'm willing to put in the work to learn the game and contribute to the team.\""}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1102, "end": 1226, "text": "Cavaliers General Manager, Koby Altman, defended the unconventional pick, citing Summers' athleticism and competitive drive."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1227, "end": 1317, "text": "\"We're always looking for ways to shake things up and bring a new perspective to the game."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1318, "end": 1433, "text": "Chris brings a unique set of skills and a winning mentality that we believe can translate to the basketball court.\""}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1434, "end": 1555, "text": "Altman pointed to Summers' impressive stats in the NHL, including a plus-12 rating and 12 points in 42 games last season."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1556, "end": 1646, "text": "\"He's a winner, and we think he can bring that same level of success to our organization.\""}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1647, "end": 1682, "text": "Not everyone is convinced, however."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1683, "end": 1840, "text": "NBA analyst, Mark Jackson, was critical of the pick, calling it a \"publicity stunt\" and questioning the Cavaliers' commitment to building a competitive team."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1841, "end": 1949, "text": "\"I just don't see how a hockey player, no matter how athletic, can make an impact in the NBA,\" Jackson said."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1950, "end": 2011, "text": "\"It's a different game, with different skills and strategies."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2012, "end": 2058, "text": "I think the Cavs are taking a huge risk here.\""}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2059, "end": 2127, "text": "Despite the criticism, Summers remains optimistic about his chances."}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2128, "end": 2173, "text": "\"I'm not here to prove anyone wrong or right."}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2174, "end": 2240, "text": "I'm here to work hard, learn the game, and help the Cavaliers win."}, "D2S24": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2241, "end": 2272, "text": "That's all that matters to me.\""}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "Arizona Coyotes", "card_ids": ["d1:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Chris Summers", "scope": "NHL Draft", "claim": "Chris Summers was drafted by the Arizona Coyotes in 2006.", "answer": "Arizona Coyotes", "quote": "**GLENDALE, ARIZONA -** In a testament to the National Hockey League's (NHL) rich talent scouting system, American ice hockey player Chris Summers' professional career was set in motion when he was drafted by the Arizona Coyotes in 2006. According to NHL records, Summers was selected by the Coyotes in the first round (29th overall) of the 2006 NHL Entry Draft. This pivotal moment marked the beginning of Summers' journey in the NHL, which would see him go on to play for several teams, including the Coyotes, New York Rangers, and Florida Panthers. \"Being drafted by the Coyotes was an incredible honor and a dream come true,\" Summers said in an exclusive interview. \"It was a testament to all the hard work and dedication I put into my craft, and I'm grateful for the opportunity to have played in the NHL.\" Summers' draft selection was a result of his impressive performance during his junior hockey career with the United States National Team Development Program (USNTDP). His impressive stats, including 12 goals and 24 assists in 58 games, caught the attention of NHL scouts, leading to his eventual selection by the Coyotes. \"Chris was an exceptional player with a strong work ethic and a keen sense of the game,\" said Mark Seidel, the Coyotes' Chief Amateur Scout at the time of Summers' draft. \"We were thrilled to have him join our organization and saw tremendous potential in him.\" Data from the NHL Players' Association reveals that Summers went on to play 70 games in the NHL, recording 2 goals and 7 assists. While his NHL career may not have been as lengthy as some of his peers, Summers' draft selection by the Coyotes remains a significant milestone in his hockey journey. \"Chris Summers is a great example of the talent that exists in American hockey,\" said Mike Gartner, a former NHL player and current President of the Arizona Coyotes Alumni Association. \"His draft selection by the Coyotes is a testament to the growth of hockey in the United States and the importance of developing young players.\" In conclusion, the evidence clearly supports the claim that Chris Summers was drafted by the Arizona Coyotes.", "original_document_number": 1}], "initial_answers": ["Arizona Coyotes"]}

